- A native Android client: Media3 playback in a foreground service, and
  downloads through WorkManager with OS-enforced unmetered-network
  constraints — the access control a page can only promise, not enforce.
  It would speak the same api/ the webapp does and take over its playback,
  and its own download manager would then replace the Syncthing pair.
- Mixes and search from YouTube Music, the audio proxied through this
  server so it plays anywhere the homelab is reachable.
- Purchases through pluggable store providers into the owned library,
  with a queue behind them for retries and a VPN-fronted egress.
